<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Prabu Siliwangi</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Prabu Siliwangi is the legendary ideal king of Pajajaran, the Sunda Kingdom of western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/java">Java</a>, and the central royal figure of Sundanese oral tradition and the bardic pantun. Popular belief often identifies him with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sri-baduga-maharaja">Sri Baduga Maharaja</a>, who reigned from 1482 to 1521, but the identification cannot be proven. His name is borne today by the Indonesian army's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-java">West Java</a> command, Kodam III/Siliwangi.</p></div>
